  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Highway, Street, and Bridge Construction (NAICS 237310) has $1.9B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. FY2026 to date totals are partial (fiscal year to date). Contracting activity includes 1,732 awards with an average award size of $1.1M, and obligations are up 57.4% year over year. Yearly obligations show fluctuation: FY21 was $1.9B, FY22 was $2.1B, FY23 was $2.8B, FY24 was $2.6B, FY25 was $1.2B, and FY26 is $1.9B. The Department of Transportation is the largest buyer with $713M in obligations, followed by the Department of Defense with $586M and the Department of Agriculture with $461M. Top vendors by obligations for FY2026 to date include KIEWIT INFRASTRUCTURE SOUTH CO at $297M, AMRIZE SOUTHWEST INC at $96.4M, and BFBC LLC at $86.3M. This profile is current through FY2026 to date and summarizes where contracting dollars and awards are concentrated in this industry.",
    "sections": [
